spans.s:
yauvan-a, n. (fr. yuvan) youth, bloom 🞄or prime of youth, adolescence, manhood: pl. 🞄youthful deeds: -darpa, m. pride of youth, 🞄juvenile indiscretion;
 -padavī, f. path of 🞄youth: -m ārūḍha, having entered on adolescence;
 🞄-prānta, m. n. end of youth;
 -vat, 🞄a. possessed of or being in the bloom of youth, 🞄youthful.
